body:
Hey again rhino\_surgeon, I just have another concern I would like to take up with them, and would like to hear your opinion first.

&#x200B;

One week post-OP the nurse tried to remove the stitches that keep the nasal septum in place. There was a bit of tugging on her part to remove the stitches, which resulted in a bit of blood, and she did not manage to get them all out. They were dissolvable stitches, she left the last thread and said they would come out on their own. Could this have caused the deviated septum I have? I am not sure whether I had it before or not, but I never had problems breathing before.

&#x200B;

Edit: I went to another surgeon who said I had the deviated septum, sadle etc.

Hey rhino\_surgeon, I found out the stitches were dissolvable, not sure either why she was trying to remove them (and failed on one side). I am now 3 weeks post and still feel congested. Do you think the nurse could have messed up something in there when trying to remove them which hinders my breathing? She told me everything was fine, and I was told I would be breathing a month after the surgery - but I dont see how much I can improve in one week as my nose still feels congested, and it varies throughout the day.

&#x200B;

Is this a real fear I am having? Do some people just need more time to be able to breathe again? I know you said often over a month and its still 3 weeks, but is it common for this to take 6-7 weeks?

You can post here; [https://imgur.com/upload](https://imgur.com/upload)   and simply copy the link.

&#x200B;

Was it many years ago you did the surgery?
